  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run (1 of 6), reporting 3 witnesses, 2 names and 1 atom read. I made no further changes after that.\n\n**Concept body** (`left_turn.lean`): the concept holds only at the observation where this becomes true:\n- the heading change over the window behind (`prim_heading_change` over `window`) is at least `turn_min` and less than `u_turn_min`, and\n- the yaw rate is at most `yaw_tol` in magnitude.\n\nThe band is signed with left positive, so a right turn and a reversal both fall outside it. If the window is truncated or a yaw rate in it is missing, the result is unknown. I declared no narrowings because every part of the body comes straight from the contract's words.\n\n**Witnesses**: one instance with window 10 s, turn_min 45°, u_turn_min 150° and yaw_tol 1 °/s. Each trace is a bicycle observed for 30 scenes, one per second.\n- **holds:** the bicycle turns at 15 °/s for 6 s, then rides straight. It is judged at 21000 ms, the first observation with zero yaw rate, where the heading change is 90°.\n- **fails:** a lane change that turns the heading +10° and back. It is judged at every observation whose window is fully covered (10000–29000 ms), and the heading change never reaches 45°.\n- **blind:** the holds trace with `kin.yaw_rate` masked, judged at 21000 ms.\n\n**One approximation in the witnesses:** the narrative says heading and yaw rate agree exactly, but headings at 5°, 10°, 15° and so on can't be written exactly as rational vectors. I rounded them to the nearest thousandth of (cos θ, sin θ). The trace check accepts this: it only flags a heading that stays the same while the yaw rate is non-zero.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
